              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وكالة — wakāla — \"an agency\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نشرت وكالة (wakāla) الأنباء الخبر صباحا. nasharat wakālat al-anbāʾ al-khabar ṣabāḥan. The news agency put out the story in the morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وكالة (wakāla) سفر: a travel agency."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وكالة (wakāla) is built on the native Arabic root w-k-l (Lane), \"to entrust an affair to someone\". A wakīl acts for others; a wakāla is the office that does."
            }
