              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أفاد — afāda — \"to give news; to be of use\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أفادت الشرطة بأن الطريق مغلق. afādat ash-shurṭa bi-anna aṭ-ṭarīq mughlaq. The police reported that the road was closed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يفيد, yufīd."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In the news: أفاد (afāda) مراسلنا بأن …, our correspondent reports that …. Elsewhere: هذا يفيد, this helps."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أفاد (afāda) is built on the native Arabic root f-y-d (Lane), where fāʾida is a gain or benefit. Form IV afāda is \"to give someone a benefit\", and so to give him information."
            }
          ]
        },
